                <pb facs="0029" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Thailand</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Chapman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-21T15:00:00+07:00">May 21, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 21—7:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. I have just been informed by a source close to the Prince Regent’s family
                    that the German Minister has promised Thailand, presumably under instructions,
                    the provinces of Kedah and Kelantan and large parts of Indo-China if Germany
                    wins the war. No <hi rendition="#italic">quid pro quo</hi> mentioned.</p>
                <p>This report not confirmed as yet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chapman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
